    {
      "id": "p0169-b006",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "The English wordplay that connects the \"Crab Apple\" name and its description would be lost in a literal translation, so the localization team relied on a more creative solution: combining the wordsfujimi (\"immortality\") and ringo (\"apple\"). The resulting name, Fujiringo, usually means \"Fuji apple\" in everyday Japanese, but instead means \"immortality apple\" in this specific, unexpected context.",
        "raw": "The English wordplay that connects the \"Crab Apple\" name and its description\nwould be lost in a literal translation, so the localization team relied on a\nmore creative solution: combining the wordsfujimi (\"immortality\") and\nringo (\"apple\"). The resulting name, Fujiringo, usually means \"Fuji apple\" in\neveryday Japanese, but instead means \"immortality apple\" in this specific,\nunexpected context.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.09112106,
          0.41665,
          0.702217,
          0.52027857
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.08903174,
          0.41593571,
          0.70428584,
          0.52135
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          27,
          28,
          29,
          30,
          31,
          32
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "名称与道具说明之间的英语文字游戏，直译会丢失。团队于是采用更有创意的办法，把日语 fujimi（不死）和 ringo（苹果）结合起来。得到的名字 Fujiringo，平时指“富士苹果”，但在这个出人意料的特定语境里，却变成了“不死苹果”。",
        "status": "draft",
